WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.450
- And the argument we had
recently, me and Lawrence,

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.313
was about oven gloves, ridiculous!

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.393
You know when you buy oven
gloves, you've got two options?

00:00:06.393 --> 00:00:08.860
Like, I like to buy the two, individual,

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.170
separate oven gloves personally.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.540
You know, one for each hand.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.410
Their independent of each
other and you're free,

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.880
as you always imagined you would be

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.045
as an adult in your own kitchen.

00:00:17.045 --> 00:00:18.310
(crowd laughing)

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.883
To move as you please.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:22.680
He gets these oven gloves where

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.360
you've still got an oven
glove for each hand,

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.970
but they're joined together
by that filthy hammock.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.970
(crowd laughing)

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.730
The most bacteria ridden bit
of fabric in your entire house.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.700
It's a quilted germ blanket.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.670
Oh, what you handling with that?

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.860
Please let it be food,
please say it's food

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.110
you're picking up with the germ cloth.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.230
I can't wait to mange
whatever it is you're cooking.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:43.980
(crowd laughing)

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.948
That's your full range
of movement with that.

00:00:51.948 --> 00:00:53.873
(crowd laughing)

00:00:53.873 --> 00:00:54.777
What is someone attacks you?

00:00:54.777 --> 00:00:56.570
You can't defend yourself.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:57.403
It could happen,

00:00:57.403 --> 00:00:58.236
just 'cause you're getting
something out of the oven

00:00:58.236 --> 00:01:00.220
doesn't mean the whole world stands still.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:01.150
What are you gonna do, garrotte them

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.182
and hope in a weeks time
they get a fungal infection?

00:01:03.182 --> 00:01:05.560
(crowd laughing)

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:06.810
They do not need to be joined together.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.020
No ones threaded those oven gloves

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:08.920
through the sleeves of their jacket

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.104
like a pair of winter
mittens to my knowledge.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.960
(crowd laughing)

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.957
Lawrence goes "They need to
be joined together, James,

00:01:15.957 --> 00:01:18.507
"so they don't get separated,
thank you very much."

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.300
They're oven gloves.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.250
They are oven gloves.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.770
Correct me if I'm wrong, they
are not leaving the kitchen.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.420
Neither one of them is
leaving the kitchen, are they?

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:31.040
There's an oven glove in the kitchen,

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:31.873
where's the other one?

00:01:31.873 --> 00:01:32.886
Probably in the kitchen.

00:01:32.886 --> 00:01:34.260
(crowd laughing)

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.730
Probably somewhere in the kitchen.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.560
No one's leaving one
oven glove by the stove

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.230
then hitting the town, solo gloving it,

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.780
like a culinary Michael
Jackson going up to people.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.730
You don't take that risk.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.267
I said to him "Man, do yourself a favor,

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.177
"take that onesie oven
glove back to the shop.

00:01:49.177 --> 00:01:51.230
"Buy yourself some proper oven gloves."

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:52.063
This is what he says.

00:01:52.063 --> 00:01:55.213
He goes "Ah, oven
gloves, shcmoven gloves."

00:01:55.213 --> 00:01:57.890
(crowd laughing)

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.137
That's how he argues
and he won, by the way.

00:02:00.137 --> 00:02:01.370
(crowd laughing)

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.153
Oven gloves, schmoven gloves,
he's won every argument

00:02:03.153 --> 00:02:04.610
we've ever had with that technique.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:06.730
Oven gloves, schmoven
gloves, bowling, schmowling,

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:08.205
cinema, schminema.

00:02:08.205 --> 00:02:09.209
(crowd laughing)

00:02:09.209 --> 00:02:11.090
The only argument he didn't
win with that was one time

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:12.848
when we argued about schmoozing.

00:02:12.848 --> 00:02:15.980
(crowd laughing)

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:19.030
If it already begins with a
schm, he ain't got nothing.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:20.520
Believe you me, when
you're leaving the house

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:21.530
off to do a bit of schmoozing

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.880
and he's shouting schmoozing,
schmoozing after you

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.263
it's more encouraging than dismissive.

00:02:25.263 --> 00:02:27.240
(crowd laughing)

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.245
Put a spring in my step.

00:02:28.245 --> 00:02:30.995
(crowd laughing)

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:34.900
Actually really good at schmoozing.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.310
I thought I'd use this
opportunity in the show

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:38.090
to give you guys some schmoozing tips.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.340
You look like some happening cats,

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:40.280
maybe you're gonna schmooze someone

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:42.350
at an office do, you know?

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:44.440
Now a lot of people tell
ya, when you're schmoozing,

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.380
have a good icebreaker.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:47.380
At the top of the conversation,
break the ice, right?

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.370
What they won't tell ya, at
the end of the conversation,

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.770
un-break the ice, right?

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:53.900
You don't want anyone else sweeping in

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.520
taking advantages of all
the lovely little ice cubes

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.801
that you created, so freeze it
over again before you leave.

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:00.550
(crowd laughing)

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.660
Just as you're leaving just
slide something under the fence

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.289
like "death comes to us
all," something like that.

00:03:04.289 --> 00:03:05.980
(crowd laughing)

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.210
Set the tone for the rest of the evening,

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:09.007
good luck anyone else
penetrating that fortress.

00:03:09.007 --> 00:03:11.757
(crowd laughing)

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:15.850
Nod a lot, when they're talking,
you do a lot of nodding,

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:17.190
that lets them know that you're listening.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.037
Every now and again just
throw in something like

00:03:19.037 --> 00:03:21.293
"Wow, I don't normally nod this much."

00:03:21.293 --> 00:03:22.520
Make them feel special.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.270
(crowd laughing)

